  "question": {
    "text": "A piece of wood of mass <math><mn>0.03</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>g</mi></math> is dropped from the top of a <math><mn>100</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>m</mi></math> height building. At the same time, a bullet of mass <math><mn>0.02</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>g</mi></math> is fired vertically upward, with a velocity <math><mn>100</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>m</mi><msup><mrow><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></math> from the ground. The bullet gets embedded in the wood. Then the maximum height to which the combined system reaches above the top of the building before falling below is: <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>m</mi><msup><mrow><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>"
